        <body>
            <div xml:id="d627">

                <pb facs="0673" n="555" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg555"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/4391: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-01T21:00:00-06:00">April 1, 1929—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 2—1:21 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>30. I have received note dated today from the Foreign Office, signed by the
                    Subsecretary: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Following instructions of His Excellency the President of the Republic,
                            I have the honor to inform Your Excellency that my Government has
                            learned, from private sources, that the North American military forces
                            in Nicaragua wish to provoke a conflict with Honduras.</p>
                        <p>My Government will be grateful to Your Excellency if you will investigate
                            this matter.</p>
                        <p>Awaiting, et cetera.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I had a conference this afternoon with the President of the Republic just before
                    this note was received and he did not mention this matter.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Managua.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
